      "period": 420,
      "seed": 11,
      "far_height": 230,
      "far_start": 700,
      "far_end": 2000,
      "far_period": 900,
      "_doc": "height/ramp/floor/period/seed: rolling hills that start at the site_rect edge; far_*: ridged hills that rise between far_start and far_end metres out so the horizon is a skyline. A look, not Rust's terrain (unverified)"
    },
    "shading": {
      "site_fade": 45,
      "site_cover": 0.32,
      "dirt_cover": 0.2,
      "macro_period": 90,
      "macro_strength": 0.22,
      "far_start": 50,
      "far_scale": 4,
      "tint_a": [
        0.8,
        0.88,
        0.66
      ],
      "tint_b": [
        0.95,
        0.9,
        0.8
      ],
      "tint_period": 260,
      "_doc": "terrain shader uniforms. site_shade darkens the site concrete patches (pale patches read as snow); tint_a/tint_b: olive and khaki colour patches over the open ground every ~tint_period metres (a look, unverified against Rust's biome colours); scrub_*: dry scrub blobs on the open ground (one per scrub_cell metres with probability scrub_density, patchy by noise, colour is an albedo multiplier); stone_*: small pale loose stones the same way. A look standing in for ground scatter we have no meshes for (unverified against Rust's arid biome). grass_*: dry green grass patches over the open ground (cover is the fraction, period the patch size in metres, colour an albedo multiplier) with a fine blade grain near the camera; rock_*: bare grey rock on hill flanks steeper than rock_slope (1 - normal.y); hill_shade: broad light and shade over the hills outside site_rect. Grass, rock and hill shade are a look standing in for Rust's splat map and grass meshes, which prep does not extract (unverified)",
